<title>SOUTH KOREA: Keopyung group wins Saehan Merchant stake auction.</title>
<headline>Keopyung group wins Saehan Merchant stake auction.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Keopyung Group has won an auction to buy a 40.6 percent stake in Saehan Merchant Banking Corp now held by Korea Development Bank (KDB) and Chemical Bank's Seoul branch, a KDB spokesman said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>Four Keopyung units, including Korea Tungsten Co and Posco Chemical Co, offered to buy Saehan's 1.79 million shares at 145 billion won, the spokesman said.</p>
<p>The price, 81,232 won per share, was more than triple the Saehan stock's closing price of 26,900 won on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Currently KDB holds a 20.45 percent stake and Chemical a 20.11 percent stake in Saehan, the spokesman said.</p>
<p>Keopyung group has 18 member companies, including three listed on the local stock market.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5646</p>
</text>
